  "title": "A rescue begins!",
  "section": "Movie Facts # 2 of 10",
  "description": "After discovering that most of the major studios had disbanded their visual effects departments, George Lucas founded his own special effects unit in 1975, Industrial Light & Magic, which began its extensive Star Wars work in a Van Nuys, California warehouse. Most of the striking visuals employed motion control photography, which created the illusion of size by employing small models and slowly moving cameras. Model starships were constructed on the basis of drawings by Joe Johnston, input from Lucas, and paintings by Ralph McQuarrie. Lucas went against the grain of traditional sci-fi by creating a \"used universe\" in which all devices, ships, and buildings looked aged and dirty"
}
